---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tools"
  description="Prototypes built because the problem was in front of me and the tool was not. Put here to find out whether they are worth anything to anyone else."
>
  <main class="reading" id="main">
    <section class="block insight-page">
      <p class="kicker">TROi</p>
      <h1>Tools</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        Working with organizations — and with a family — produces a long list of things you wish existed while
        you were standing in front of the problem. This is where I build them.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most of what lands here is in ideation, prototype or early beta. Several of them already run on my own
        machine and solve my own problem every day, which is exactly the point at which it becomes impossible
        to tell whether they are useful or merely mine.
      </p>

      <p>
        So I put them up. If one of them is worth something to someone besides me, I would rather find out
        now than after another six months of building. The three faces at the bottom of each page are for
        that, and they take one press: they tell me what to take further and what to let mature a while
        longer. If you have more to say than a face can carry, <a href="/contact/">write to me</a>.
      </p>

      <ul class="tool-list">
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Working prototype</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/cambium/">Cambium</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            Most architecture tools draw what an organization has. This one draws what it costs to get
            something through it.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Part built, part specified</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/flowlens/">FlowLens</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            Work/life balance metrics on the wrist. Four questions about the week that people already ask
            themselves and mostly answer by guessing, answered from your own history.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Built, not yet worn</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/flowmission/">FlowMission</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            An hour in a city you don't know, or a race you have a time for. The watch works out what is
            possible and hands back one instruction, plus a promise that you get back — and somebody who is
            told when you don't.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Working prototype</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/livspusslet/">Livspusslet</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            A household runs on a plan that lives in one person's head. This puts the year on a page instead
            — clickable, in Swedish.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Working prototype</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/bordvakt/">Bordvakt</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            Some restaurants release a month of tables in one batch and lose them in minutes. This waits for
            the release.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .tool-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0;
  }
  .tool-list li {
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--mist);
  }
  .tool-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--mist);
  }
  .tool-name {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .tool-line {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
</style>
